            "review_title": "Review at Botejyu Okonomiyaki",
            "review_text": "Edmund K\nSingapore, Singapore2883 contributions\n0\nGood quality and tasty curry pork katsu\nJan 2025 • Solo\nI did not plan to eat Japanese food in Vietnam. I have had my chance to eat aplenty in Japan.\n\nStumbled upon Botejyu during the walk around of Vincom's lower ground level, my curiosity was piqued by a description of its founder. This is not your usual Japanese restaurant. Judging from its history, it is rather classy.\n\nI ordered pork katsu curry with rice and miso. The pork was fresh and curry tasty. I can vouch for its authentic gohan and pure miso. The aroma was thrilling.\n\nNormally, I gobble up a meal when hungry. But I did not want the moment to go to waste. I savoured the dish spoon-by-spoon, sip-by-sip. \n\nJapanese food cannot be eaten fast food style.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2025",
